#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507461 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078604 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cff76d55-4647-547b-af6d-959810d2b8e2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Square Root of a Number Using a Tangent Line Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62e9b3b4-caa5-543b-b91f-58e818cef373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{1}{12}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62e9b3b4-caa5-543b-b91f-58e818cef373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{1}{12}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506913} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd1d6034-d9bb-50d2-ab93-d34b4b0eeb0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9928af49-cfd1-5831-93d9-b7e47b2c04f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-348182" :question/problem "Determine the tangent line approximation $L(x)$ of $\\sqrt{x}$ at $x=36.$\n\n$L(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $x=a$ is\n\n$$\nL(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=36,$ which gives\n\n$$\nL(x)=f(36)+{f}^{′}(36)(x-36).\n$$\n\nLet's compute $f(36)$ and ${f}^{′}(36)$ in the expression above. Evaluating the function, we get\n\n$$\nf(36)=\\sqrt{36}=6,\n$$\n\nand computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}},\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(36)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{36}}=\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 6}=\\frac{1}{12}.\n$$\n\nSo, the tangent line approximation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(36)+{f}^{′}(36)(x-36) \\\\  & =6+\\frac{1}{12}(x-36) \\\\  & =6+\\frac{1}{12}x-3 \\\\  & =6-3+\\frac{1}{12}x \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{12}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078604 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cff76d55-4647-547b-af6d-959810d2b8e2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Square Root of a Number Using a Tangent Line Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de6f8be6-6596-58af-9ce5-a41ed5840d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de6f8be6-6596-58af-9ce5-a41ed5840d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507159} :answer-field/id #uuid "966c34db-6e27-5dd8-a0ad-ccae600f29f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4db89f44-88ed-5c90-a196-4f35357b51b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-348190" :question/problem "Approximate the value of $\\sqrt{2}$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\sqrt{2}≈$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $x=a$ is\n\n$$\nL(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=1,$ which gives\n\n$$\nL(x)=f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1).\n$$\n\nLet's compute $f(1)$ and ${f}^{′}(1)$ in the expression above. Evaluating the function, we get\n\n$$\nf(1)=\\sqrt{1}=1,\n$$\n\nand computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}},\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the tangent line approximation is\n\n$$\nL(x)=1+\\frac{1}{2}(x-1).\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $\\sqrt{2}$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & ≈L(2) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{2}(2-1) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0899ab8c-7841-5824-b954-76481006bd7e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Cube Root of a Number Using a Tangent Line Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cff4156-737c-5680-b33d-fdb1d68a8c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506785} {:answer/id #uuid "5986235a-2921-5759-a191-af2a18fdbc09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{82}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506885} {:answer/id #uuid "883bd3ae-28da-510c-841c-e4785fb12348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506980} {:answer/id #uuid "8b07f807-b49e-5325-87cc-64297c9d06c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506987} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa3e5d8-774f-584c-8335-89acba32ff13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{79}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5986235a-2921-5759-a191-af2a18fdbc09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{82}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506885} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5e247f-a4ec-5159-bfa6-d891f0df4964" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0a9d3c2-a748-522d-b588-6439a04ab73d" :question/math-academy-id "q-48022" :question/problem "Using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ at $x=27$, approximate the value of $\\sqrt[3]{28}.$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $x=a$ is\n\n$$\nL(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=27,$ which gives\n\n$$\nL(x)=f(27)+{f}^{′}(27)(x-27).\n$$\n\nLet's compute $f(27)$ and ${f}^{′}(27)$ in the expression above. Evaluating the function, we get\n\n$$\nf(27)=\\sqrt[3]{27}=3,\n$$\n\nand computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt[3]{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(27)=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{27}^{2}}}=\\frac{1}{27}.\n$$\n\nSo, the tangent line approximation is\n\n$$\nL(x)=3+\\frac{1}{27}(x-27).\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $\\sqrt[3]{28}$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=28.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{28} & ≈L(28) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{27}(28-27) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{27}(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{82}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0899ab8c-7841-5824-b954-76481006bd7e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Cube Root of a Number Using a Tangent Line Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a2976a0-0da2-51e3-b607-e3b7fdf48e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L(x)=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{12}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506984} {:answer/id #uuid "aa64d5c8-6b2c-5400-ab54-479b918ae1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L(x)=\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{1}{12}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507055} {:answer/id #uuid "b299ba6d-15a7-5206-93b4-ddf6e7762462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L(x)=2+\\frac{1}{12}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507072} {:answer/id #uuid "e1031c62-6f4c-541f-a9db-838853dc81dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L(x)=4+\\frac{1}{10}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507167} {:answer/id #uuid "fabfba2e-0dc4-5aff-af52-07bd79cb9842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L(x)=\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{10}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a2976a0-0da2-51e3-b607-e3b7fdf48e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L(x)=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{12}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506984} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4bafff-98ce-522c-801e-5469e85e7f5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37b97735-c2a7-51cf-8f02-b676a9408bdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-48026" :question/problem "What is the tangent line approximation of $\\sqrt[3]{x}$ at $x=8?$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $x=a$ is\n\n$$\nL(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=8,$ which gives\n\n$$\nL(x)=f(8)+{f}^{′}(8)(x-8).\n$$\n\nLet's compute $f(8)$ and ${f}^{′}(8)$ in the expression above. Evaluating the function, we get\n\n$$\nf(8)=\\sqrt[3]{8}=2,\n$$\n\nand computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt[3]{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(8)=\\frac{1}{3{(\\sqrt[3]{8})}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{12}.\n$$\n\nSo, the tangent line approximation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(8)+{f}^{′}(8)(x-8) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{12}(x-8) \\\\  & =2+\\frac{1}{12}x-\\frac{8}{12} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{12}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{12}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078605 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0899ab8c-7841-5824-b954-76481006bd7e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Cube Root of a Number Using a Tangent Line Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "294f5786-0f39-547c-b630-ed2166d78751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506772} {:answer/id #uuid "2a947bee-66a0-5a69-98c8-44c523b82d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506777} {:answer/id #uuid "427332ff-d010-54dd-bbfe-c47060010871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506833} {:answer/id #uuid "62a7abe2-e0d6-55fe-9e3c-db0416ab8fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506912} {:answer/id #uuid "8add4622-a34d-581b-99af-045a8face06c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "427332ff-d010-54dd-bbfe-c47060010871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506833} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d783028-76a3-5726-8b6d-65c9752085e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73785757-6df7-5674-90c2-d6eaa9a04258" :question/math-academy-id "q-86438" :question/problem "Approximate the value of $\\,2\\sqrt[3]{8.9}\\,$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)=2\\sqrt[3]{x}\\,$ at $\\,x=8.$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $x=a$ is\n\n$$\nL(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=8,$ which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x)=f(8)+{f}^{′}(8)(x-8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $f(8)$ and ${f}^{′}(8)$ in the expression above. Evaluating the function, we get\n\n$$\nf(8)=2\\sqrt[3]{8}=4,\n$$\n\nand computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt[3]{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich in turn, gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(8)=\\frac{2}{3{(\\sqrt[3]{8})}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nSo the tangent line approximation is\n\n$$\nL(x)=4+\\frac{1}{6}(x-8).\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $2\\sqrt[3]{8.9}$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=8.9.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt[3]{8.9} & ≈L(8.9) \\\\  & =4+\\frac{1}{6}(8.9-8) \\\\  & =4+\\frac{1}{6}(0.9) \\\\  & =4+0.15 \\\\  & =4.15\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
